A note on NoDerivatives, because it is a real consequence and not boilerplate

ND blocks redistributing a modified version of the work. It does NOT stop
you reading, running or learning from this code, and it does not stop you
making a private fork to understand it.

It does stop two things that a reader may reasonably want:

  — You cannot open a pull request against this repository that changes
    the code, because that is proposing a redistributable derivative. If
    you find a bug, please open an issue describing it rather than a PR.
  — You cannot publish your own copy with changes in it.

That is deliberate. This repository exists to demonstrate how I build
systems, and the demonstration is the authorship. If you want to build
something from these ideas, the architecture is documented in docs/ with
its reasoning and its alternatives — build your own, tell me about it, and
I will be genuinely pleased.

For a licence that permits modifications while still barring commercial
use, CC BY-NC 4.0 is the one to ask for.
